[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The board layout condenses cycles before assigning stable layers

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-LAYOUT
TITLE: The board layout condenses cycles before assigning stable layers
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
layout.js treats the snapshot as a directed multigraph. It condenses strongly
connected components, ranks the resulting acyclic projection from left to
right, orders each rank with deterministic barycentric sweeps, and keeps every
original node and edge for rendering. The layout consumes and returns
application-owned objects so Dagre or ELK can replace it later.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ported 2026-09-01 from the codex spike byte-identical. Its measured shape
there: the real snapshot condensed to 348 strongly connected components with
two two-node cycles preserved; oversized logical ranks pack into at most 32
rows per adjacent lane.
<<<
